  "notes": "ケア comes from English \"care\" and is used both as a noun and as a suru verb (ケア⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧).\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- スキンケア: skincare\n- ヘアケア: hair care\n- メンタルケア: mental health care\n- ⟦{介護|かいご}→介護：04805_kaigo⟧ケア: nursing care\n- アフターケア: aftercare, follow-up care\n- セルフケア: self-care\n- ケアマネージャー: care manager (in nursing/welfare)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{手入|てい}れ→手入れ：07178_teire⟧: maintenance, grooming (more traditional Japanese term)\n- ⟦{介護|かいご}→介護：04805_kaigo⟧: nursing care (specifically for elderly/disabled, more formal)\n- ⟦{世話|せわ}→世話：02088_sewa⟧: taking care of, looking after (broader, everyday term)",
